## Phaser-Specific Notes

1. Use Phaser's preload method for primary asset loading:
   ```typescript
   preload(): void {
     // Always load critical assets in preload
     this.load.image('player', 'assets/player.png');
     this.load.spritesheet('explosion', 'assets/explosion.png', { 
       frameWidth: 64, frameHeight: 64 
     });
   }
   ```

2. Leverage Phaser's loading events for progress tracking:
   ```typescript
   // Set up loading events
   this.load.on('progress', (value: number) => {
     // Update progress bar with percentage
     progressBar.clear();
     progressBar.fillRect(x, y, width * value, height);
   });
   
   this.load.on('complete', () => {
     // Loading complete, clean up listeners
     progressBar.destroy();
     this.load.off('progress');
   });
   ```

3. Use Phaser's built-in cache for efficient resource management:
   ```typescript
   // Check if asset is already in cache
   if (this.textures.exists('enemy')) {
     // Use existing texture
   } else {
     // Load it
     this.load.image('enemy', 'assets/enemy.png');
   }
   
   // Access cached data
   const cachedTexture = this.textures.get('player');
   ```

4. For dynamic loading after game start, use loader in separate scenes:
   ```typescript
   // Show loading scene for mid-game asset loading
   this.scene.launch('DynamicLoader', { 
     assets: ['level2_map', 'level2_enemies'],
     onComplete: () => {
       this.scene.stop('DynamicLoader');
       this.startLevel2();
     }
   });
   